 d consulting program where IU students from across majors and class years
  work in teams on real-world international development projects. Consulta
 nts collaborate with global partner organizations\, tackle complex challe
 nges\, and gain hands-on experience that goes far beyond the classroom.</
 p><p><strong>Through GDC\, you can:</strong></p><ul><li>Work on real inte
 rnational development projects  </li><li>Collaborate with organizations a
 nd partners around the world  </li><li>Build consulting\, research\, proj
 ect management\, and communication skills  </li><li>Learn about global ch
 allenges across regions and sectors  </li><li>Join a multidisciplinary co
 mmunity of students from across IU  </li><li>Grow into leadership roles o
 ver multiple years in the Lab  </li></ul><p><strong>No prior consulting o
 r international development experience is required.</strong> If you're cu
 rious about global issues and want to put your skills to work on meaningf
 ul projects\, come learn what GDC is all about.</p><p>  **must be able to
  attend weekly meetings on Fridays from 1:55-3:55</p><p>  Ready to apply?
