LOCATION:Hamilton Lugar School
SUMMARY:CLACS Global Health Series Workshop with Charlotte Scott: Introdu
 ction to Implementation Research in a Global Health Setting 
DESCRIPTION:CLACS Global Health Workshop with Charlotte Scott (https://fa
 irbanks.indianapolis.iu.edu/about/directory/scott-charlotte.html)\, MSc  
 Lecturer\, Community and Global HealthSchool of Public Health\, Indiana U
 niversity Indianapolis  How do we move effective public health interventi
 ons from research into real-world practice and make sure they work within
  the communities they are intended to serve?  Join the Center for Latin A
 merican and Caribbean Studies (CLACS) for a Global Health Series Workshop
  with Charlotte Scott\, MSc\, Lecturer in Community and Global Health at 
 the IU Richard M. Fairbanks School of Public Health.Implementation resear
 ch is a field that is still growing\, but it is a key contributor to effe
 ctive global health programs and policies\, as well as individual practic
 es. Implementation research identifies and investigates problems that pre
 vent effective implementation of interventions\, develops and tests imple
 mentation strategies that provide solutions to these implementation probl
 ems\, and obtains information to guide scale-up and sustainability. Its f
 ocus is on real-world conditions\, aiming to work with the intended popul
 ation\, in the specific context\, and under the actual influential factor
 s. This workshop will offer an introduction to the topic and an opportuni
 ty to reflect on these concepts with a real-world example.&#160\;  Scott 
 brings extensive experience working in Colombia. Before joining IU\, she 
 worked with the International Center for Medical Training and Research (C
 IDEIM) and the Social Innovation in Health Initiative (SIHI) in Cali\, Co
 lombia contributing to community-based health research and public health 
 training.  &#160\;About the CLACS Global Health Series  The CLACS Global 
 Health Series brings together students\, faculty\, practitioners\, and co
 mmunity members to explore health challenges and public health initiative
 s across Latin America and the Caribbean. Developed in coordination with 
 Whitney Cordoba-Grueso\, MD\, PhD\, MPH\, the series connects regional kn
 owledge with interdisciplinary perspectives on global health\, including 
 mental and reproductive health\, infectious and chronic disease\, migrati
 on\, environmental health\, and health equity.This event is free and open
  to everyone. Students\, faculty\, staff\, and members of the wider commu
 nity are welcome.Planning to attend?  Please register using the button be
 low. Registration is requested to assist organizers with planning.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p data-pm-slice="1 1 []"><strong>CLACS Glob
 al Health Workshop with <a href="https://fairbanks.indianapolis.iu.edu/ab
 out/directory/scott-charlotte.html">Charlotte Scott</a>\, MSc</strong><br
  />  Lecturer\, Community and Global Health<br /><strong>School of Public
  Health\, Indiana University Indianapolis</strong></p><p>  How do we move
  effective public health interventions from research into real-world prac
 tice and make sure they work within the communities they are intended to 
 serve?</p><p>  Join the <strong>Center for Latin American and Caribbean S
 tudies (CLACS)</strong> for a <strong>Global Health Series Workshop</stro
 ng> with <strong>Charlotte Scott</strong>\, MSc\, Lecturer in Community a
 nd Global Health at the IU Richard M. Fairbanks School of Public Health.<
 /p><p><strong data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody"></strong>Implementation 
 research is a field that is still growing\, but it is a key contributor t
 o effective global health programs and policies\, as well as individual p
 ractices. Implementation research identifies and investigates problems th
 at prevent effective implementation of interventions\, develops and tests
  implementation strategies that provide solutions to these implementation
  problems\, and obtains information to guide scale-up and sustainability.
  Its focus is on real-world conditions\, aiming to work with the intended
  population\, in the specific context\, and under the actual influential 
 factors. This workshop will offer an introduction to the topic and an opp
 ortunity to reflect on these concepts with a real-world example.&#160\;</
 p><p>  Scott brings extensive experience working in Colombia. Before join
 ing IU\, she worked with the <strong>International Center for Medical Tra
 ining and Research</strong> (CIDEIM) and the <strong>Social Innovation in
  Health Initiative</strong> (SIHI) in Cali\, Colombia contributing to com
 munity-based health research and public health training.</p><p><picture><
