SUMMARY:A conversation on the geopolitics of Mongolia by Jargal Defacto
DESCRIPTION:Mr. Jargalsaikhan Dambadarjaa (known as Jargal DeFacto) is an
  independent economist and media representative of Mongolia. He is a Mong
 olian political and economic observer\, columnist\, and host of TV's Defa
 cto Debate\, Defacto Review\, and Defacto Interview\, weekly television i
 nterviews on VTV in Mongolia\, featuring distinguished Mongolian\, Englis
 h- and Russian-speaking guests from across the globe. Jargal also hosts R
 adio DeFacto\, a radio talk show aired daily at 6:30 pm on Business Radio
  98.9FM.  He is a founder of The Defacto Institute\, an independent resea
 rch think tank that also publishes The Defacto Gazette\, a weekly analyti
 cal newspaper covering the politics and economics of Mongolia—in Englis
 h\, Japanese\, and Mongolian.  In this talk\, Jargal Defacto will share h
 is perspective on the geopolitics of Mongolia as a journalist. The talk w
 ill be moderated by David Bosco\, Interim Dean of the Hamilton Lugar Scho
 ol.This event will take place both on Zoom and in person.This event is sp
 onsored by:Department of Central Eurasian Studies (CEUS)The Inner Asian a
 nd Uralic National Resource Center (IAUNRC)The East Asian Studies Center 
 (EASC)The Byrnes Institute (REEI)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Mr. Jargalsaikhan Dambadarjaa (known as
  Jargal DeFacto) is an independent economist and media representative of 
 Mongolia. He is a Mongolian political and economic observer\, columnist\,
  and host of TV's Defacto Debate\, Defacto Review\, and Defacto Interview
 \, weekly television interviews on VTV in Mongolia\, featuring distinguis
 hed Mongolian\, English- and Russian-speaking guests from across the glob
 e. Jargal also hosts Radio DeFacto\, a radio talk show aired daily at 6:3
 0 pm on Business Radio 98.9FM.</p><p>  He is a founder of The Defacto Ins
 titute\, an independent research think tank that also publishes The Defac
 to Gazette\, a weekly analytical newspaper covering the politics and econ
 omics of Mongolia—in English\, Japanese\, and Mongolian.</p><p>  In thi
 s talk\, Jargal Defacto will share his perspective on the geopolitics of 
 Mongolia as a journalist. The talk will be moderated by David Bosco\, Int
 erim Dean of the Hamilton Lugar School.</p><p><strong>This event will tak
 e place both on Zoom and in person.</strong></p><p><em>This event is spon
