SUMMARY:Lifeline: The Story of PEPFAR Fireside Chat
DESCRIPTION:Join the Indiana University Center for Global Health (https:/
 /globalhealth.iu.edu/) for a Fireside Chat with global health leaders and
  author John Donnelly. Donnelly will discuss his new book "Lifeline: The 
 Story of PEPFAR\, the Greatest Humanitarian Initiative of Our Time" (http
 s://www.johndonnellyauthor.com/) .  Hoosiers played a key role in the est
 ablishment and success of PEPFAR. Ambassador Randy Tobias\, first U.S. Gl
 obal AIDS Coordinator\; IU Center for Global Health director Dr. Adrian G
 ardner\; and leaders from AMPATH Kenya's HIV program\, one of the first a
 nd most successful PEPFAR partners\, will be in attendance to add to the 
 conversation.  When President George W. Bush launched the President's Eme
 rgency Plan for AIDS Relief (PEPFAR) in 2003 in response to the AIDS cris
 is devastating sub-Saharan Africa\, millions of people were dying every y
 ear and entire nations were being destabilized by the pandemic. Over the 
 next two decades\, PEPFAR saved more than 26 million lives\, prevented ne
 arly 8 million infant HIV infections\, strengthened health systems\, and 
 helped bolster economies and governments across Africa.  Drawing on a wea
 lth of internal documents and interviews with more than 200 participants\
 , Lifeline reveals how an unlikely coalition of leaders and advocates ove
 rcame political\, logistical\, and cultural obstacles to build a program 
 many thought was impossible. John Donnelly is uniquely positioned to chro
 nicle this history. As a reporter for The Boston Globe\, he spent more th
 an a decade covering AIDS policy and America's response to the epidemic\,
  living in South Africa and reporting across the continent during PEPFAR'
 s formative years.  Attendees can pre-order a signed copy of John Donnell
 y's new book "Lifeline" to pick up at the event. Please visit Golden Hour
  Books (https://www.goldenhourbooks.net/item/1sM1NJwkMQeztDkePKtpUQ) webs
 ite to order and indicate that you will pick up at the event.  Light snac
 ks will be served.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join the <a title="https://globalhealth
 .iu.edu/" href="https://globalhealth.iu.edu/" target="_blank" rel="nofoll
 ow noopener noreferrer" data-msys-clicktrack="0">Indiana University Cente
 r for Global Health</a> for a Fireside Chat with global health leaders an
 d author John Donnelly. Donnelly will discuss his new book <a title="http
 s://www.johndonnellyauthor.com/" href="https://www.johndonnellyauthor.com
 /" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" data-msys-clicktrac
 k="0">"Lifeline: The Story of PEPFAR\, the Greatest Humanitarian Initiati
 ve of Our Time"</a> .</p><p>  Hoosiers played a key role in the establish
 ment and success of PEPFAR. Ambassador Randy Tobias\, first U.S. Global A
 IDS Coordinator\; IU Center for Global Health director Dr. Adrian Gardner
 \; and leaders from AMPATH Kenya's HIV program\, one of the first and mos
 t successful PEPFAR partners\, will be in attendance to add to the conver
 sation.</p><p>  When President George W. Bush launched the President's Em
 ergency Plan for AIDS Relief (PEPFAR) in 2003 in response to the AIDS cri
 sis devastating sub-Saharan Africa\, millions of people were dying every 
 year and entire nations were being destabilized by the pandemic. Over the
  next two decades\, PEPFAR saved more than 26 million lives\, prevented n
 early 8 million infant HIV infections\, strengthened health systems\, and
  helped bolster economies and governments across Africa.</p><p>  Drawing 
 on a wealth of internal documents and interviews with more than 200 parti
 cipants\, Lifeline reveals how an unlikely coalition of leaders and advoc
 ates overcame political\, logistical\, and cultural obstacles to build a 
 program many thought was impossible. John Donnelly is uniquely positioned
  to chronicle this history. As a reporter for <em>The Boston Globe</em>\,
  he spent more than a decade covering AIDS policy and America's response 
 to the epidemic\, living in South Africa and reporting across the contine
 nt during PEPFAR's formative years.</p><p>  Attendees can pre-order a sig
 ned copy of John Donnelly's new book "Lifeline" to pick up at the event. 
 Please visit <a title="https://www.goldenhourbooks.net/item/1sM1NJwkMQezt
 DkePKtpUQ" href="https://www.goldenhourbooks.net/item/1sM1NJwkMQeztDkePKt
 pUQ" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" data-msys-clicktr
 ack="0">Golden Hour Books</a> website to order and indicate that you will
  pick up at the event.</p><p>  Light snacks will be served.</p>
UID:20261020T220000Z-2402253@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20260831T153520Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2398640-lifeline-the-story-of-pepfa
 r-fireside-chat
LAST-MODIFIED:20260831T193520Z
