X-SOURCE:IU Hamilton Lugar School
DTSTART:20261022T203000Z
DTEND:20261022T213000Z
LOCATION:Hamilton Lugar School (355 N Eagleson Ave)
SUMMARY:Career Pathways with former Diplomat Katherine Ntiamoah
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in navigating federal and international ca
 reer pathways\, developing practical tradecraft\, and learning how to lev
 erage your network?  &#160\;  Join us for this week's ASP Pathways sessio
 n featuring Katherine A. Ntiamoah\, Director of Policy Engagement and Str
 ategic Partnerships at the Hamilton Lugar School and a former U.S. Diplom
 at. Drawing on her diverse career spanning diplomacy\, Capitol Hill\, cam
 paigns\, and public policy\, Katherine will break down the real-world tra
 decraft needed to break into international affairs and foreign service.  
 Whether you are mapping out your coursework\, looking for high-impact int
 ernships\, or trying to figure out what comes after graduation\, this ses
 sion offers a candid\, practical look at building a high-stakes career in
  diplomacy and global policy.  This event is open to Undergraduate and gr
 aduate students interested in African Studies\, Global Studies\, internat
 ional relations\, and public service.&#160\;
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Are you interested in navigating federa
 l and international career pathways\, developing practical tradecraft\, a
 nd learning how to leverage your network?</p><p>  &#160\;</p><p>  Join us
  for this week's <strong>ASP Pathways</strong> session featuring <strong>
 Katherine A. Ntiamoah</strong>\, Director of Policy Engagement and Strate
 gic Partnerships at the Hamilton Lugar School and a former U.S. Diplomat.
  Drawing on her diverse career spanning diplomacy\, Capitol Hill\, campai
 gns\, and public policy\, Katherine will break down the real-world tradec
 raft needed to break into international affairs and foreign service.</p><
 p>  Whether you are mapping out your coursework\, looking for high-impact
  internships\, or trying to figure out what comes after graduation\, this
  session offers a candid\, practical look at building a high-stakes caree
 r in diplomacy and global policy.</p><p>  This event is open to Undergrad
 uate and graduate students interested in African Studies\, Global Studies
 \, international relations\, and public service.&#160\;</p>
UID:20261022T203000Z-2438225@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20261002T161346Z
