SUMMARY:What's happening at the COP31 climate summit?
DESCRIPTION:This November\, delegates from around the world will gather t
 o attend the Conference of the Parties (COP) and take stock of global pro
 gress on addressing climate change and to seek pathways toward greater cl
 imate action. The conference is convened under the United Nations Framewo
 rk Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC) to measure progress and negotiat
 e the best ways to address climate change. Parties decide how to cut gree
 nhouse gas emissions and adapt to the impacts of climate change\, on Loss
  and Damage\, and on the means to help countries green their economies an
 d build resilience to climate change.  Join ERI to hear from members of t
 he IU student delegation who are participating in COP31 as observers and 
 researchers. Learn about the stakes of this year's conference as well as 
 insights gathered from attendees at this global event.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  This November\, delegates from around t
 he world will gather to attend the Conference of the Parties (COP) and ta
 ke stock of global progress on addressing climate change and to seek path
 ways toward greater climate action. The conference is convened under the 
 United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC) to measure
  progress and negotiate the best ways to address climate change. Parties 
 decide how to cut greenhouse gas emissions and adapt to the impacts of cl
 imate change\, on Loss and Damage\, and on the means to help countries gr
 een their economies and build resilience to climate change.</p><p>  Join 
 ERI to hear from members of the IU student delegation who are participati
 ng in COP31 as observers and researchers. Learn about the stakes of this 
 year's conference as well as insights gathered from attendees at this glo
 bal event.</p>
UID:20261111T170000Z-2428208@events.iu.edu
